YANI: adding mid-game challenge, penalizing dawdling

Sure. Perhaps a "turns (ever) on this level"
counter, that ups the average difficulty of monsters
generated every N additional turns [and perhaps also
improves the equipage of those monsters]?

Pudding farming, credit cloning without a magic
whistle, other time consuming occupations, or just
plain dawdling, could become a _lot_ more expensive
that way.

One could also just do that with the existing turns
counter, but making it level-specific adds a bit of
zest at the expense of some extra code and an
additional data structure or structure field for the
turns-on-this-level count.

As a separate mechanism, if one were _really_
malicious [like, oh, say, our beloved DevTeam], one
could just add (increasingly nasty) traps to a level
every so often _during play_, not just at level
generation time, so that the longer one stayed, the
more dangerous navigation became, and so that
previous knowledge of safe passage decayed with
time, sort of like a slow acting amnesia spell.

Slowly filling the level in with rock as time passes
could be fun, too, so that what starts as a navigable
maze, stops being one if you stall around too much,
passages slowly disappear, and so on.

